### Family Care API - Auth endpoints
### How to use: install the VS Code extension "REST Client" (humao.rest-client),
### then click the "Send Request" link that appears above each request.
### Run #1 (register) or #2 (login) first — the tokens are captured automatically
### into variables and reused by the requests below.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000/api/v1
@email = john.doe@example.com
@password = StrongP@ss1

### 1. Register (default role FAMILY_MANAGER)
# @name register
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}",
  "fullName": "John Doe"
}

### 2. Login
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### Capture tokens from the login (or register) response
@accessToken = {{login.response.body.data.accessToken}}
@refreshToken = {{login.response.body.data.refreshToken}}

### 3. Get current user (protected)
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 4. Refresh tokens (rotation)
# @name refresh
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{refreshToken}}"
}

### 5. Logout (protected) — clears the stored refresh token
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### --- Negative cases ---

### 6. Weak password -> 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "weak@example.com",
  "password": "123"
}

### 7. Wrong password -> 401
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "WrongPass1!"
}

### 8. No token -> 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
